course: dictionary
lesson: 5443
title: Names with capital letters
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A capital letter at the start of a word is a clue that it is a name, not an ordinary word. Lancaster can name a place, a royal family, a plane, or a person. The words around it tell you which one. «Some castles really were prisons: the Tower of London held famous prisoners for hundreds of years, and Lancaster Castle was still used as a prison until 2011.» The castle is a place, so Lancaster is naming a place here.
explain: Ask yourself: is this a place, a person, or a thing? Then look at the nearby words. Castle sits next to Lancaster, so it must be a place. If the sentence said «the red rose» or «the Wars of the Roses», you would know it means the royal family, not the city.
explain: Names can be the same word in different places. Lancaster is a city, but it is also a surname, like the American actor Burt Lancaster. Context tells you which Lancaster is meant, so always check the sentence before you decide.
fact: Lancaster is a city in north-west England, and it is the county town of Lancashire.
fact: The House of Lancaster was a royal family of England, whose sign was the red rose.
fact: The House of Lancaster fought the House of York in the Wars of the Roses, from 1455 to 1487.
fact: The Wars of the Roses ended when Henry Tudor won, so the Lancaster and York families were no longer fighting for the crown.
fact: The Lancaster was a famous British bomber plane of the Second World War, and Lancaster is also a surname.
exercise: In «Lancaster Castle was still used as a prison until 2011», what kind of name is Lancaster? | A type of food | A kind of bird | *A place name | A word meaning red
exercise: Which flower was the sign of the House of Lancaster? | The sunflower | The white rose | *The red rose | The daisy
exercise: Lancaster is the county town of which county? | Cornwall | Yorkshire | *Lancashire | Kent
test: Which war was fought between the House of Lancaster and the House of York? | The Battle of Hastings | The Second World War | *The Wars of the Roses | The Great Fire of London
test: What was the Lancaster in the history of Britain? | A river in Italy | A type of red rose | *A famous British bomber plane of the Second World War | A castle in Scotland
exam: Which city in north-west England has a castle and a university? | Exeter | Leeds | Brighton | *Lancaster
